  "title": "What underwriters actually decide before they start underwriting",
  "summary": "Before any rater opens, commercial underwriters run a quiet first-pass judgment on a submission that shapes how much time, attention, and benefit-of-the-doubt the file receives. In a softening property market and hardening casualty market, that invisible read is moving quote ratios, hit ratios, and the mix of business that makes it to bind.",
